    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for the kind of sweet potato power bowl the clean-eating spots price at $13. Yours has more meat and no line at lunch.",
    "shop_smart":  "Sweet potatoes are the biggest line across about 9 lbs. Loose sweet potatoes by the pound usually beat the bagged ones here, so check both tags.\nSalsa from the jar covers tomatoes, onion, and chiles in one pour. Store brand on sale drops it cheaper still.\nLight sour cream costs the same as full fat and trims the calories for free. The 5 lb turkey pack keeps the meat price per pound down.",
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Heat the oven to 425F. Scrub and dice the sweet potatoes into half-inch cubes, toss with the olive oil, salt, and black pepper, and spread on sheet pans.",
                    "Roast 25 to 30 minutes, flipping once, until browned at the edges and tender in the middle.",
                    "While they roast, brown the ground turkey in a big skillet, breaking it up, until it reaches 165F with no pink remaining.",
